export anchor MiniDashboardsStyle:
    number: 196
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Mini dashboards
    idea: Every project gets its own small dashboard tile, with a status chip, a sparkline of this week's completions and three stats in a ruled footer, so the home screen reads as a wall of six comparable instruments.
    base: light
    palette:
        canvas: #f1f3f7, the page behind the tiles
        tile: #ffffff, tiles, the rail, panels and fields
        ink: #182033, text and figures
        muted: #556075, labels, meta and axis text
        line: #dfe3ea, tile borders and stat dividers, never text
        violet: #5b3fc4, the primary button, sparklines, this week bars, progress edges and focus
        violetTint: #efebfc, the current nav item, sparkline areas and last week bar fills
        green: #18794e, On track with a check disc on #e3f3ea
        amber: #8a5a00, At risk with a diamond on #fbf0d9
        red: #c0272d, Behind with a down triangle and overdue figures on #fbe7e7
    type:
        One stack, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Ubuntu, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial. The greeting is 22px bold, strip figures 22px bold tabular,
        tile stats 20px bold with a 12px muted unit, tile names 16px bold,
        body 14px, and stat labels 11px semibold caps tracked 0.04em.
    layout:
        An 80px white icon rail on the left holds a violet square logo of
        four tiles, six nav items with an icon over a small label, Home in
        a violet tint, and initials at the foot. The main area opens with
        a greeting line that holds Hello, Mara, the brand, the date and a
        red clock note for the 4 overdue tasks, with a search field, a
        violet New project button, a bell and Mara Okafor at the right. A
        single white strip splits the four summary numbers into cells with
        tinted icon squares, the overdue cell red. The projects band is a
        three by two grid of tiles in due date order. Each tile has the
        team label, the project name and a status chip on top, then a
        violet sparkline of tasks done per day this week beside a large
        violet count of done this week, then a ruled three cell footer of
        Complete, Tasks and Due with days left, and a 4px progress edge
        along the base in violet, amber or red. Below, a two to one split
        puts a 14 day bar chart, last week as outlined tint bars and this
        week as solid violet split by a dashed divider with values on top,
        beside an activity panel with coloured initial discs. Below 1100px
        tiles go two across, and on phones the rail becomes a scrolling top
        bar and tiles stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px gaps between and inside tiles and 24px between bands.
    density: Medium high. Six instruments at once, each with a chart and three numbers.
    corners: 12px tiles and panels, 10px controls and rail items, 6px chips and 3px bars.
    borders: A 1px cool grey border on every tile, ruled stat footers and a 4px progress edge at the base.
    shadows: One soft pair, 0 1px 2px and 0 2px 8px at 5 to 6 percent ink.
    icons:
        Round line icons at 1.8px with labels in the rail. Status is a
        solid check disc, diamond with a bang or down triangle in a tinted
        chip with its word.
    focus: A solid 2px violet outline offset 2px, and a violet tint on a focused list row.
    tone: Instrument labels, such as Complete, Tasks, Due 14 Nov and 7 done this week.
